# Hilt (DevSpeak)

```
di/
├── AppModule.kt
├── DispatcherModule.kt
├── NetworkModule.kt       # OkHttp only (SSE Phase 2)
├── SupabaseModule.kt      # supabase-kt Auth + Postgrest
├── RepositoryModule.kt    # @Binds interface → Impl
├── DataStoreModule.kt     # healthtrack_prefs
└── DatabaseModule.kt      # Room
```

Do **not** add Retrofit or Moshi. `DataStoreModule` and `DatabaseModule` are both required.

SDK types (`SupabaseClient`, `Auth`, `Postgrest`) are provided in `SupabaseModule` and consumed only by `data/`. ViewModels inject UseCases (or domain repository interfaces), never `SupabaseClient`.

## NetworkModule — OkHttp

```kotlin
@Module
@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)
object NetworkModule {

    @Provides
    @Singleton
    fun provideOkHttpClient(): OkHttpClient = OkHttpClient.Builder()
        .connectTimeout(Constants.TIMEOUT_SECONDS, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
        .readTimeout(Constants.TIMEOUT_SECONDS, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
        .addInterceptor(
            HttpLoggingInterceptor().apply {
                level = HttpLoggingInterceptor.Level.BASIC
            },
        )
        .build()
}
```

Do not share this client with Ktor. Do not put `BASE_URL` / API keys in `Constants`.

## SupabaseModule

URL and publishable/anon key from `BuildConfig` (`local.properties`). Never `service_role`.

```kotlin
@Module
@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)
object SupabaseModule {

    @Provides
    @Singleton
    fun provideSupabaseClient(): SupabaseClient = createSupabaseClient(
        supabaseUrl = BuildConfig.SUPABASE_URL,
        supabaseKey = BuildConfig.SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY,
    ) {
        install(Auth) {
            autoLoadFromStorage = true
            alwaysAutoRefresh = true
            autoSaveToStorage = true
        }
        install(Postgrest)
    }

    @Provides
    @Singleton
    fun provideAuth(client: SupabaseClient): Auth = client.auth

    @Provides
    @Singleton
    fun providePostgrest(client: SupabaseClient): Postgrest = client.postgrest
}
```

Do **not** `install(ComposeAuth)`, `realtime-kt`, `functions-kt`, or `storage-kt` until that phase.

## RepositoryModule

```kotlin
@Module
@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)
abstract class RepositoryModule {

    @Binds
    @Singleton
    abstract fun bindAuthRepository(impl: AuthRepositoryImpl): AuthRepository

    @Binds
    @Singleton
    abstract fun bindProfileRepository(impl: ProfileRepositoryImpl): ProfileRepository
}
```

Remote data sources use `@Inject constructor` — no extra module.

## DispatcherModule

```kotlin
@Provides
@Singleton
fun provideAppDispatcher(): AppDispatcher = AppDispatcher(
    io = Dispatchers.IO,
    main = Dispatchers.Main,
    default = Dispatchers.Default,
)
```

## ViewModel

```kotlin
@HiltViewModel
class SignInViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val signInWithEmail: SignInWithEmailUseCase,
    private val dispatcher: AppDispatcher,
) : ViewModel()
```

## Scopes

| Scope | Use for |
|---|---|
| `@Singleton` | `SupabaseClient`, OkHttp, DataStore, repositories |
| `@Inject` on data source | Fine with `@Singleton` on the class |
| `@ViewModelScoped` | Rare; prefer `viewModelScope` |
